{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 32, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a Count of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187 he was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. He became the Count of Tripoli after the death of his father in 1152. \n*Early Life* \nRaymond III was born in 1140 to Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem his mother was the daughter of Baldwin II King of Jerusalem and Morphia of Melitene. He had a younger sister Melisende who married the lord of Sidon. \n*Reign* \nRaymond III became the Count of Tripoli in 1152 after the death of his father he was only 12 years old at that time. The regency was held by the King of Jerusalem Baldwin III who was also his cousin. In 1155 Raymond III was declared to be of age and he took over the control of the county. \n*Imprisonment and Release* \nIn 1164 Raymond III was captured by Nur ad-Din the atabeg of Aleppo during a battle he was imprisoned for several years. He was released in 1173 after paying a large ransom. After his release he married Hodierna's niece also named Hodierna. \n*Later Life and Death* \nRaymond III played a significant role in the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Crusader army was defeated by Saladin the Sultan of Egypt and Syria. He escaped from the battle and fled to the city of Tyre. He died in 1187 shortly after the battle. \n*Succession* \nRaymond III did not have any children so the county of Tripoli was inherited by his nephew Raymond of Antioch who was the son of his sister Melisende. \n*Legacy* \nRaymond III was known for his bravery and military skills he was also a skilled politician who maintained good relations with the other Crusader states and the Byzantine Empire. He also played a significant role in the politics of the Kingdom of Jerusalem and was a close ally of the King of Jerusalem Amalric I.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -9.775113539944869e-06}, {"tok